---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Odoo vs ERPNext — Which Is Right for Your Business? | Ecosoft"
  description="An honest comparison of Odoo Community Edition and ERPNext from a consultancy that implements both — covering modules, customisation, cost, and which suits different business types."
>


  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom:2rem;">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Resources</p>
      <h1>Odoo vs ERPNext — an honest comparison from a firm that implements both.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">
        Most comparisons are written by companies that sell only one platform. We implement both.
        This is our honest assessment of when each platform is the right choice — and when it isn't.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SUMMARY VERDICT -->
  <section class="section" style="background: var(--surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(280px, 100%), 1fr)); gap:2rem; max-width:900px; margin:0 auto;">
        <div class="info-card" style="border-top: 4px solid #1a56db; padding:2rem;">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Choose Odoo if…</h3>
          <ul style="list-style:none; padding:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:0.5rem;">
            <li>✓ You're a manufacturer with complex BOM requirements</li>
            <li>✓ You have a large sales team needing CRM + sales management</li>
            <li>✓ You need a wide range of OCA community modules</li>
            <li>✓ You want maximum flexibility for future customisation</li>
            <li>✓ You're a government agency needing Thai public sector compliance</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card" style="border-top: 4px solid #3b82f6; padding:2rem;">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Choose ERPNext if…</h3>
          <ul style="list-style:none; padding:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:0.5rem;">
            <li>✓ You're a project-based business (services, consulting, aerospace)</li>
            <li>✓ Your team is technically sophisticated and values developer tooling</li>
            <li>✓ You want Python-native customisation via server scripts</li>
            <li>✓ You need strong HR, payroll, and leave management out of the box</li>
            <li>✓ You want a fully integrated helpdesk and CRM without extra modules</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- COMPARISON TABLE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="text-align:center;">Feature comparison</h2>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto; margin-top:2rem;">
        <table class="pricing-table" style="width:100%;">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Feature / Criterion</th>
              <th>Odoo CE + OCA</th>
              <th>ERPNext</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Licence</td>
              <td>LGPL (free, open-source)</td>
              <td>GPL / MIT (free, open-source)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Per-user cost</td>
              <td>None</td>
              <td>None</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Manufacturing / BOM</td>
              <td>✓ Excellent — OCA adds depth</td>
              <td>✓ Good — strong for project-based</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Project management</td>
              <td>Basic</td>
              <td>✓ Strong — native project billing</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>CRM & Sales</td>
              <td>✓ Excellent</td>
              <td>Good</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>HR & Payroll</td>
              <td>Good (OCA modules)</td>
              <td>✓ Strong — built-in payroll engine</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Accounting</td>
              <td>✓ Excellent — Thai OCA modules</td>
              <td>✓ Good — Thai compliance available</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Government ERP modules</td>
              <td>✓ Available (Ecosoft-built)</td>
              <td>Not available</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Developer experience</td>
              <td>Python / XML / OWL</td>
              <td>✓ Python / Jinja — more accessible</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>REST API</td>
              <td>✓ Comprehensive</td>
              <td>✓ Comprehensive + webhooks</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Community size</td>
              <td>✓ Larger — OCA alone has 3,500+ modules</td>
              <td>Smaller but active</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Module upgrade path</td>
              <td>Annual major versions</td>
              <td>Annual major versions</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Best for industries</td>
              <td>Manufacturing, Trading, Government</td>
              <td>Technology, Services, Healthcare</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="pricing-note" style="text-align:center; margin-top:1.5rem;">
        This comparison covers Odoo Community Edition + OCA modules and ERPNext. Odoo Enterprise is a separate, paid product — Ecosoft implements Community Edition only.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- DEEPER DIVE -->
  <section class="section" style="background: var(--surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width:760px; margin:0 auto; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:2rem;">
        <div>
          <h2>The module ecosystem difference</h2>
          <p>
            Odoo's OCA (Odoo Community Association) maintains over 3,500 open-source modules across hundreds of repositories.
            This is a significant advantage for complex or unusual requirements — there is likely an existing OCA module
            for most things, reducing custom development cost.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem;">
            ERPNext's community app ecosystem is smaller but growing. The advantage of ERPNext is that the core system
            covers more ground natively — HR, payroll, project management, and helpdesk are all built in without needing
            additional modules.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>Customisation philosophy</h2>
          <p>
            Both platforms support custom development — but the experience differs. Odoo customisation uses Python,
            XML/QWeb, and OWL JavaScript, following the Odoo module inheritance pattern.
            ERPNext customisation uses Python, Jinja templates, and Frappe's DocType system,
            with server scripts providing a more accessible customisation layer for simpler cases.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem;">
            For sophisticated technical teams, both are viable. For businesses without in-house developers who want
            to make lightweight changes without engaging a consultant, ERPNext's server script approach is more accessible.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>Thai compliance</h2>
          <p>
            Both platforms have Thai accounting compliance available. For Odoo, the Thai localisation is maintained
            by the OCA Thai community, and Ecosoft has contributed directly. For ERPNext, Thai compliance is available
            through community and Ecosoft-maintained modules.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem;">
            For government-specific compliance (budget encumbrance, government procurement), Odoo with Ecosoft's
            custom modules is the only viable open-source option in Thailand — ERPNext government modules don't exist.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-strip">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Still not sure which platform is right for you?</h2>
      <p>Tell us about your business and requirements. We'll give you a direct recommendation — not a sales pitch for the platform we prefer to implement.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get a Platform Recommendation</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
